WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.740
Over the last 15 years I've probably hired
tens of thousands of people that I've worked

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.070
with and when you work with these different
personalities, there are a lot of things that

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:14.080
you can measure, but there are a lot of things
that you cannot measure, whatsoever.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:20.190
And the only way you can measure this is through
seeing this person go through it and how they

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.690
respond to it.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.620
In an interview, a person can impress you
a lot.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.220
"Oh my gosh, I've done this, I've done that,"
and then you get to work and you realize who

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.220
the real person is.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:36.010
So I'm going to talk about 10 Unmeasurable
Qualities of a Human Being in this video today.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.660
You can pretty much create an opinion for
yourself on when you're hiring people, and

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:45.620
working with people, or even yourself on which
of these areas really is this person extremely

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.690
strong at.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:48.489
So let me get right into it.

00:00:48.489 --> 00:00:50.430
Ten unmeasurable.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:55.090
#1 to me is heartbeat of an organization.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:58.140
Let me explain what I mean by heartbeat of
an organization.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:05.360
You'll get somebody in and they'll start working
and let's say they're working in a department

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.210
or an office together and you know, within
a month, two months, three months, and all

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.770
of a sudden, they become a heartbeat of the
organization.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.909
No one knows it.

00:01:11.909 --> 00:01:15.170
When Mario first got started [you guys know
who Mario is], when Mario first got started

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:19.380
with me, we had a meeting within two weeks
we had a sales meeting on Monday morning at

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.189
like 8:00 and he had only been there for two
weeks.

00:01:22.189 --> 00:01:23.590
It was the first time he came there.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.869
And somebody made a remark about another one
of our sales people in our office, sales managers

00:01:26.869 --> 00:01:27.899
in our office.

00:01:27.899 --> 00:01:29.630
So these two sales managers got into it.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:34.060
Mario got up and he said, "Look, I don't know
who you are, but you just don't talk to a

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.070
lady like that."

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.090
He had only been there for two weeks.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.090
Boom!

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.329
Immediately we found out a lot about him,
two weeks into it.

00:01:41.329 --> 00:01:42.630
He became the heartbeat.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:47.919
From thereon, everybody knew that when this
cat was around, people were protected because

00:01:47.919 --> 00:01:49.770
he protected people.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:50.770
That's a heartbeat, right?

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.840
But you don't know that right off the bat
when you're working with somebody.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.920
If somebody can be a heartbeat of an organization.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.899
Whenever you look at a heartbeat of a sports
team, you'll learn, somebody comes out of

00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:02.159
nowhere when it's tough, it's playoffs, they
show up.

00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:04.739
But you didn't know it in practice, they don't
show up.

00:02:04.739 --> 00:02:05.739
That's heartbeat.

00:02:05.739 --> 00:02:09.780
You won't know that part until there's time
that goes by and there are situations for

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.780
them to rise up.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:11.780
#2:Vision

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:13.530
A lot of people talk about, "I have a very
big vision."

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:14.530
A grand vision.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.099
I want to do this, I want to do that.

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:22.019
But they get this much success and you realize
their vision is a very small vision.

00:02:22.019 --> 00:02:26.599
Vision takes a long time for somebody to realize
if this person has vision or not.

00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:30.730
I've hired people who say, "Oh, long term
I want to see myself doing this with the company

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:33.099
and I want to run this department, I want
to do this" and then you realize they get

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:36.200
a little bit of money and boom, they're vision
gets smaller and smaller and smaller.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.200
You don't see it any more.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.370
And then there are certain people that you
may not hear anything about them and what

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:44.959
they say, and then one time they said something
about a vision and the next thing you know,

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:49.689
they're responding and delivering in a way
that they have a bigger vision than people

00:02:49.689 --> 00:02:52.870
that have been there for six years.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:53.900
Six years!

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.939
They're just constantly going to chase the
vision that they have in their lives.

00:02:57.939 --> 00:03:02.579
You cannot measure somebody's vision, by saying,
"tell me about your vision."

00:03:02.579 --> 00:03:03.579
#3:Desire

00:03:03.579 --> 00:03:10.799
Desire is, I mean, if there was a mechanism
that came out that scanned people and said,

00:03:10.799 --> 00:03:15.459
"he has desire at the highest level," or,
"this guy has no desire whatsoever," it would

00:03:15.459 --> 00:03:21.829
save thousands, billions of hours for different
CEOs and companies to know who to work with

00:03:21.829 --> 00:03:28.450
and who not to work with, because desire on
somebody wanting it so bad, want it SO bad.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:33.269
You know, "Pat, you have no idea how bad I
want to win. . . " and then boom, one thing

00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:34.980
happens and they quit.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.290
"Oh, you don't know what just happened.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:37.629
We had a family crisis."

00:03:37.629 --> 00:03:38.780
What's the crisis?

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:42.959
"We had my 7th cousin that just got into an
accident."

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:44.140
Family crisis?

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.870
"Yeah, you don't understand because I had
to go and.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:50.629
. . " One time, twice, and every time something
happens, they're gone for a week.

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:51.629
Okay?

00:03:51.629 --> 00:03:52.939
This person doesn't have any desire.

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:55.019
They're just talking a big game.

00:03:55.019 --> 00:03:56.890
Everything to them is a family crisis.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:57.890
They don't have desire.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:59.439
You'll learn about it when you work with them.

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:02.280
You work with someone and say, "This cat's
got a lot of desire as well.'

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.280
#4: Ambition

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:06.050
I want to move up in the company, I want to
be a leader.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.989
I want to do this, I want to do that.

00:04:07.989 --> 00:04:08.989
Okay, great.

00:04:08.989 --> 00:04:09.989
We'll see.

00:04:09.989 --> 00:04:10.989
And you realize, they're very ambitious.

00:04:10.989 --> 00:04:12.689
They're there first thing in the morning,
they leave late, they work, nobody tells them

00:04:12.689 --> 00:04:15.370
to stay late, they're getting things done,
they're doing stuff.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.820
They're absolutely ambitious.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.260
You learn about them a year, two years, three
years, four years, five years.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.870
. . this is one of the most ambitious people
I've ever met.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.310
And they're not slowing down.

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:23.440
They're not slowing down.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.810
You can't measure someone's ambition by just
looking at them.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:28.810
#5:Long-Term Thinking

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.819
A lot of people are short-term thinkers.

00:04:30.819 --> 00:04:31.819
Most people are short-term.

00:04:31.819 --> 00:04:34.560
If something doesn't work out for 30, 60 days,
"You know, this is not working, I'm going

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.560
to bail.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:36.940
I'm going to go somewhere else."

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:40.479
Long-term thinking is someone who says, "I
don't know why, but I get the feeling these

00:04:40.479 --> 00:04:41.550
guys are going places.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:46.620
I don't know why, but I see that long-term
I can be a leader and I'm going to come out

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:49.389
here and be a big part of this organization."

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:51.490
Long-term thinking.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.090
Long-term thinking.

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:56.500
Long-term thinking there is no way in the
world you're going to know if this person

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:00.099
has long-term thinking or short-term thinking
until you hire the person.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.380
Okay, next one.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.669
Tenacity/thick skin, right?

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:07.220
You'll hire certain people and they look good,
they're sharp, everything is good about them,

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:11.060
but you say the smallest challenge to them
and they're like, "Oh my gosh," and they shut

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.130
down.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:13.210
Whoa.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:17.570
If you are that thin skinned, what are you
going to do when the customer berates you

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:20.480
on a call and absolutely goes off on you.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:22.349
You're going to be afraid of the phones.

00:05:22.349 --> 00:05:25.341
Oh, thin skinned, you're not thick skinned,
we learn about you.

00:05:25.341 --> 00:05:26.810
You're going to be soft and sensitive.

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:30.449
This is either not the right department for
you, or this is not the right company for

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:31.449
you.

00:05:31.449 --> 00:05:33.849
Or you got to work on becoming thicker skinned
and become the stronger leader.

00:05:33.849 --> 00:05:35.650
But we have to do one of those three, right?

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:37.200
You'll learn about that with time with people.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.069
Next is loyalty.

00:05:39.069 --> 00:05:40.069
Loyalty is purely time.

00:05:40.069 --> 00:05:41.460
All these things take time.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:45.289
Every single one of these takes time to realize
who's loyal and who's not.

00:05:45.289 --> 00:05:49.360
You realize who's in it just for them and
who's in it for the entire organization.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:54.230
Loyalty to me is a very big thing because
it doesn't take thousands of people to create

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:56.040
a major, major movement.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:01.250
It takes a handful of people that are absolutely
loyal to you who are ambitious, driven, desire,

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:05.060
big thinkers, big vision, long-term thinking,
that have bought into what you want to do,

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:08.540
that are willing to do whatever they can to
run through the wall for this cause to become

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:12.349
a reality, for you to build a massive conglomerate
for yourself.

00:06:12.349 --> 00:06:14.669
But it does take finding the right loyal people.

00:06:14.669 --> 00:06:15.669
#8: Creativity

00:06:15.669 --> 00:06:17.419
"I'm very creative.

00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:18.419
I'm an artist.

00:06:18.419 --> 00:06:19.419
I've been painting all my life.

00:06:19.419 --> 00:06:20.419
I'm about music.

00:06:20.419 --> 00:06:21.419
I'm about this.

00:06:21.419 --> 00:06:22.419
. . " Okay, great.

00:06:22.419 --> 00:06:24.259
Then you have an innovation meeting together
to come up with ideas.

00:06:24.259 --> 00:06:26.080
"What ideas do you have?"

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.080
"Umm.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.560
. . have you guys thought about putting up
a box."

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.100
Put up a box?

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:31.650
Yeah, what if we put up a box?"

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:35.690
What do you mean put up a box?

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:39.010
Have you guys thought about doing such and
such to the website?

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:41.440
It's like a bland idea.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:44.490
And you sit there and after one, two, three,
four meetings and there are no ideas.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:45.810
This person is not creative.

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:47.729
You are not creative.

00:06:47.729 --> 00:06:50.349
It takes time to find out who is creative
or not.

00:06:50.349 --> 00:06:53.129
Point #9 is how competitive they are.

00:06:53.129 --> 00:06:54.639
You hear a lot of people who say, "I'm very
competitive.

00:06:54.639 --> 00:06:55.639
I want to move up.

00:06:55.639 --> 00:06:56.639
I'm very, very competitive.

00:06:56.639 --> 00:06:58.449
I'm the most competitive person I know."

00:06:58.449 --> 00:07:00.560
And then you bring them in and they're really
not that competitive.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.150
If they lose, they're okay with it.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.900
They lose twice, they're okay with it.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.009
They don't have this desire to come in, stay
late, show up on the weekend to want to really

00:07:08.009 --> 00:07:10.680
improve and go back and take the weekend and
study and improve their craft.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:11.680
They don't have that.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:15.449
And then you have somebody that comes in that's
quiet and doesn't look like a competitor that's

00:07:15.449 --> 00:07:17.349
absolutely competitive.

00:07:17.349 --> 00:07:19.849
They take the weekend to improve, they come
back sharper in a meeting.

00:07:19.849 --> 00:07:20.849
They're ready.

00:07:20.849 --> 00:07:21.849
You see they improved.

00:07:21.849 --> 00:07:22.849
They got better.

00:07:22.849 --> 00:07:25.030
You can't tell if somebody is competitive
or not right off the bat.

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:28.320
And the last one I'll put in is hard working.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:32.020
I've had a lot of people I've hired over the
years that say, "I'm the hardest working person

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:33.020
I know.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:34.629
I'm the hardest working person I know.

00:07:34.629 --> 00:07:36.560
I'm the hardest working person I know."

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:38.439
And then they can't wait to go home at 5:00.

00:07:38.439 --> 00:07:40.360
That's not the hardest working person you
know.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:44.090
There's a lot more harder working people than
you if you can't wait to go home at 5:00.

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:48.199
"But you know, I have to go home.

00:07:48.199 --> 00:07:49.199
Something came up."

00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:51.620
Okay, a second time, third time, fourth time.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:52.620
Constantly.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:55.949
It's Friday, I have to leave at 3:00 and then
you see them come Monday to work and their

00:07:55.949 --> 00:07:59.439
face is so red because they went golfing the
entire time.

00:07:59.439 --> 00:08:05.139
So all those sorts of things you see on the
hard work side and the competitive side, you

00:08:05.139 --> 00:08:06.520
can't measure these types of things.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.009
No matter who you hire, you can't measure.

00:08:08.009 --> 00:08:12.229
The only way, the only thing that you have
to figure out these things where you can measure

00:08:12.229 --> 00:08:13.229
it is time.

00:08:13.229 --> 00:08:16.790
Time is the only thing you have when you hire
somebody to find out what their heartbeat

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:22.949
is, their real vision, the desire, the ambition,
how long-term thinking they are, how thick-skinned

00:08:22.949 --> 00:08:27.160
they are, tenacity, loyalty, creativity, how
competitive they are, and how hard working

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:28.160
you are.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:33.430
The only thing you have as you are working
with them is to pay very close attention to

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:39.380
these areas and hopefully they have enough
tests that you can put to see if they truly

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:41.050
have these things.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:44.750
You as a leader can test these areas to find
out [snap] yep, they have it.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:45.890
[Snap] No, don't have it.

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:46.990
[Snap] No, don't have it.

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:48.070
[Snap] Yes, they have it again.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:50.100
[Snap] Yes, they have it again.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:53.871
This is real because three times I tested
the same area and the person has it.

00:08:53.871 --> 00:08:58.800
And you as a leader find out about these areas
by certain tests you give them when you're

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.620
working with these folks and that's a whole
different subject that we can get on.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:04.030
But anyway, That's my message to you.

